{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>For HaShem's portion is His people.</b> Why all this? Because His portion was held among them and destined to emerge — and who is His portion? <b>His people.</b> And who is His people?" "<b>Yaakov the cord of His inheritance.</b> And he is the third of the fathers, tripled in three merits — the merit of his father's father, the merit of his father, and his own merit — behold, three, like this cord that is made of three strands. And he and his sons were His inheritance — not Yishmael son of Avraham, and not Esav son of Yitzchak (cf. Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:11.002337998Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}